1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,940
Do you like shopping?
你喜欢购物吗？

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:07,710
For shopaholics in the UK, the place to head to used to be the ‘high street’.
对于英国的购物狂来说，过去最值得去的地方是“商业街”（high street）。

3
00:00:07,710 --> 00:00:16,580
This location refers to the streets in the centre of a town where businesses and popular branches of retail chains could be found.
这个地方指的是城镇中心的街道，那里有各类商铺和热门零售连锁店的分店。

4
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:22,960
It was the place where you could find familiar fashion brands and essential everyday items.
在那里，你能找到熟悉的时尚品牌和必备的日常用品。

5
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:28,900
But change in our shopping habits has taken its toll on the British high street.
但我们购物习惯的改变，已经给英国商业街带来了沉重打击。

6
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:33,680
News about shops losing money and shutting is now common.
如今，商店亏损倒闭的新闻屡见不鲜。

7
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:43,470
Some city-centre department stores have closed and even long-established retailers such as Marks and Spencer have reported profit slumps.
一些市中心的百货公司已经关门，甚至像玛莎百货（Marks and Spencer）这样历史悠久的零售商也报告了利润下滑。

8
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:56,620
According to the accountancy firm Pricewaterhouse Coopers and the Local Data Company, a record 2,481 shops disappeared from UK high streets last year - up by 40%.
据普华永道会计师事务所和本地数据公司统计，去年英国商业街消失的商店数量达到了创纪录的2481家，同比增长40%。

9
00:00:56,620 --> 00:01:04,930
Even some large warehouse-style stores in out-of-town retail parks, have gone bust and shut up shop.
甚至一些位于城郊零售园区的大型仓储式商店也纷纷破产歇业。

10
00:01:04,930 --> 00:01:12,630
As the BBC’s Emma Simpson writes, things have become a lot harder for traditional retailers in recent years.
正如英国广播公司的艾玛·辛普森所写，近年来传统零售商的日子变得艰难多了。

11
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:20,320
They have faced rising costs from wages, business rates and the requirement to introduce Europe’s new data law.
他们面临着工资、商业税率上涨以及欧盟新数据法实施带来的成本压力。

12
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:23,950
But the biggest threat has come from online shopping.
但最大的威胁来自网购。

13
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:38,510
She says “Consumers now spend one in every five pounds online - and if businesses are seeing 20% fewer sales on the shop floor, as well as their fixed costs rising, then profit margins will be squeezed.”
她说：“现在消费者每花5英镑，就有1英镑是在网上消费的——如果商家的线下销售额下降20%，同时固定成本上升，那么利润率就会受到挤压。”

14
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:50,790
While some of us like to window shop – browsing for things to buy, only to purchase them online at a discount - the fact is that, overall, shoppers are making fewer visits to high streets.
虽然我们中有些人喜欢只看不买——浏览想买的东西，最后却在网上打折购买——但事实是，总体而言，消费者去商业街的次数越来越少。

15
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:55,100
Eventually, town centres could become like ghost towns.
最终，城镇中心可能会变成“鬼城”。

16
00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:02,740
If people aren’t out and about shopping, they won’t use other services, like cafes, restaurants and cinemas.
如果人们不外出购物，就不会光顾咖啡馆、餐厅、电影院等其他服务场所。

17
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:05,710
It also results in job losses.
这也会导致失业。

18
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:14,920
The British Retail Consortium has already warned that 900,000 UK retail jobs could be lost by 2025.
英国零售协会已经警告，到2025年，英国零售业可能会失去90万个工作岗位。

19
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:27,030
The high street has also suffered from the advent of big shopping malls, which offer a retail experience under one roof, with free parking, away from the bad weather!
此外，大型购物中心的出现也让商业街雪上加霜——这些购物中心提供一站式购物体验，有免费停车服务，远离恶劣天气！

20
00:02:27,030 --> 00:02:32,360
Meanwhile, back on the high street, some shops still exist.
与此同时，商业街仍有一些商店在苦苦支撑。

21
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:38,510
Analysts have said it’s those that have moved away from traditional retailing that are surviving.
分析师表示，那些摆脱传统零售模式的店铺才能存活下来。

22
00:02:38,510 --> 00:02:49,620
These include beauty salons, nail bars and independent coffee shops – but are these kinds of shops enough to keep the British high street open for business?
其中包括美容院、美甲店和独立咖啡馆——但这些类型的店铺，是否足以让英国商业街继续运营下去呢？
